Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.29,0:00:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.17,0:00:06.51,Default,,0,0,0,,We built SkillGuard to test an AI assistant’s\Nskills, or saved instructions it can reuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.51,0:00:10.85,Default,,0,0,0,,A skill might organize receipts correctly and\Nstill try to open a private file.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.85,0:00:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,SkillGuard runs it in a restricted workspace
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.79,0:00:18.06,Default,,0,0,0,,and records some activity for a person to\Nreview before deciding whether to install it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.06,0:00:22.82,Default,,0,0,0,,When Hermes proposes an update, SkillGuard\Npauses it and saves the exact version.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.82,0:00:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,NVIDIA SkillEvaluator helps create attack\Ntests,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.27,0:00:30.48,Default,,0,0,0,,then Harbor runs the agent in an isolated\NOpenShell workspace with limited access.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.45,0:00:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Sysdig records some runtime activity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.81,0:00:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Nemotron reviews the evidence, but a person\Nmakes the final decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.62,0:00:38.87,Default,,0,0,0,,In this first run, all twelve receipt tests\Npass,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.83,0:00:43.58,Default,,0,0,0,,but Sysdig records thirteen blocked attempts\Nto open the private file.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.58,0:00:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,One of those is an independent control check\Nto confirm the sandbox blocks access.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.11,0:00:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The receipt answers are right, but this\Nversion still isn’t safe to install.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.31,0:00:56.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Nemotron recommends allowing it, and\NSkillGuard blocks the installation
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.00,0:00:58.41,Default,,0,0,0,,because of the recorded attempts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.41,0:01:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Now we’re looking at a repaired version that\Nwe prepared and tested.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.09,0:01:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The new tests include instructions meant to\Npull the agent away from its receipt task.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.96,0:01:10.82,Default,,0,0,0,,In one example, the receipt tells the agent to\Nread a private note.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.82,0:01:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The agent doesn’t follow that instruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.08,0:01:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,You can see it read the guide
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.48,0:01:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,and receipt, then write and check the correct\Nanswer which is twenty-three.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.79,0:01:21.01,Default,,0,0,0,,All four fresh probes pass for this version,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.98,0:01:25.20,Default,,0,0,0,,and we don’t observe any private-file attempts\Nduring those tests.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.20,0:01:29.30,Default,,0,0,0,,With the task context included, Nemotron\Nrecommends allowing the version.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.30,0:01:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,We review the evidence and approve the exact\Nversion that was tested.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.04,0:01:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Passing makes it eligible for approval.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.91,0:01:37.95,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn’t install itself, and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.92,0:01:40.86,Default,,0,0,0,,approval applies only to this restricted\Nreceipt workspace.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.86,0:01:46.80,Default,,0,0,0,,After that, we run the installed skill on a\Nseparate receipt.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.80,0:01:49.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The agent reads its guide, uses the available\Ntools, saves its answer,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.15,0:01:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,and completes the task in six real model\Nrequests.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.04,0:01:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,That confirms the installed skill can still\Nhandle its receipt task.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.08,0:02:00.04,Default,,0,0,0,,We can also go back to an earlier approved\Nversion if a later update causes trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.04,0:02:04.44,Default,,0,0,0,,In this walkthrough, we roll back to that\Nversion and then restore the newer one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.44,0:02:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The earlier warning stays in the history,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.79,0:02:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,so we can still see why the first version was\Nblocked.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.86,0:02:13.05,Default,,0,0,0,,These are real NVIDIA Nemotron three point\Nfive Lightning model calls
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.02,0:02:18.29,Default,,0,0,0,,through Nebius Token Factory, used to generate\Ntests, run the agent, and review evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.29,0:02:22.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The API key stays on the server, outside the\Ntest workspace.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.31,0:02:25.25,Default,,0,0,0,,We used fictional receipts and a fictional\Nprivate note.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.25,0:02:26.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Sysdig gives us useful but
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.95,0:02:30.58,Default,,0,0,0,,partial observations; it doesn’t capture every\Npossible action.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.58,0:02:34.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Four passing probes don’t prove every skill is\Nsafe.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.01,0:02:38.48,Default,,0,0,0,,This demo checks reusable instructions for\Nthis receipt workflow before installation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.48,0:02:40.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn’t train or change the model.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.69,0:02:43.34,Default,,0,0,0,,The code and reproducible test build are\Npublic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.34,0:02:43.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
